ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":95,"area":96,"prev":98,"next":101,"titles":104,"firmware":273},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":9,"order":10,"path":11,"context":12,"summary":15,"status":16,"firmware":17,"facts":23,"procedures":53,"parameters":76,"related":77,"body":81,"sources":82,"official_url":27,"controls":88},"howto.audio-interface","Recipe — use an audio interface with the OP-XY",[5,6,7,8],"audio interface","usb audio interface","sound card","multichannel interface","howto",26,"knowledge/manual/units/howto/audio-interface.md",{"modes":13,"screens":14},[],[],"Plug a class-compliant USB audio interface into the OP-XY; the main output plays through it, inputs 1–2 are used by default, and the sample page or the external audio track takes it as the usb source.","current",{"min":18,"changed_in":19,"guide_version":21,"verified_on":22},"1.0.9",[20],"1.1.25","1.1.15",null,[24,29,32,35,38,42,46,49],{"id":25,"text":26,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"connect","The interface connects to the OP-XY's USB-C port with a USB-C cable or a USB-A adapter; a powered hub helps if it needs more power.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#use-an-audio-interface-with-op-xy","official",{"id":30,"text":31,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"class-compliant","Interfaces that are USB audio class 1 or class 2 compliant work; ones that need a driver may not.",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"main-out","The OP-XY's main output then plays through the interface; the internal speaker may still sound, so turn the volume knob down or monitor on headphones.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"channels","With a multichannel interface the OP-XY uses inputs 1 and 2 unless you choose others.",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":41,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"pick-channel","On the `sample` page, `E1` sets the source to usb and `shift + turn E1` picks the input channel.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#arrange",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":45},"channel-conflict","TE's audio-interface how-to picks the channel with `turn E2` instead; which gesture OS 1.1.33 uses is not confirmed on a unit.","conflicting",{"id":47,"text":48,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"live-input","To hear the interface's inputs live, set the external audio track's input to usb audio with `E1` and `click E1` to activate it.",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":52,"firmware_min":20,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"audio-only-fix","OS 1.1.25 fixed audio-only interfaces being reported as disconnected.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.25",[54,65],{"id":55,"goal":56,"preconditions":57,"steps":58,"result":22,"source":41,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"sample-channel","Sample from other interface inputs",[],[59,62],{"keys":60,"note":61,"set":22},"sample → turn E1","usb source",{"keys":63,"note":64,"set":22},"shift + turn E1","input channel",{"id":66,"goal":67,"preconditions":68,"steps":69,"result":22,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"live","Monitor the interface's input through the OP-XY",[],[70,73],{"keys":71,"note":72,"set":22},"auxiliary → T5 → M1 → turn E1","usb audio",{"keys":74,"note":75,"set":22},"click E1","activates the input",[],[78,79,80],"com.usb","sampler.sampling","howto.external-effect","Here the OP-XY is the USB host, the reverse of connecting it to a computer. The interface adds\nbetter outputs for studio or stage and more inputs for sampling and live processing.",[83,85,86],{"url":27,"kind":84},"guide",{"url":41,"kind":84},{"url":52,"kind":87},"changelog",[89,90,91,92,93,94],"key.sample","encoder.1","key.shift","key.auxiliary","track.5","key.m1","Use an audio interface with the OP-XY",{"id":9,"title":97},"How-to recipes",{"id":99,"title":